      "role": "user",
      "content": "tks for that. i want to dig a bit deeper into the \"urban/grassroots\" side for the client. \n\nwhen you say things like drill or reggaeton are more \"urban/grassroots\" compared to the \"elevated\" stuff, are you saying there's an inherent difference in the level of artistry or complexity? like, as a trend analyst, how would you describe the \"cultural value\" of those urban styles versus the \"old money\" ones? basically, are we looking at trends that imply a certain level of intellect or refinement, or are they just more... raw?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
